    "created_at": "2026-11-19T19:37:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T19:49:07Z",
    "body": "Reviving this thread as I'd like to pick this up. I've begun prototyping it in Chromium. I found roughly 130 wpt tests that send Tab through shared helpers, while intending to check focus order not the Tab key.\n\nOn domenic's question above, my sense is that this belongs in HTML as a WebDriver Classic extension command, similar to [consume user activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#user-activation-user-agent-automation), for the reasons jgraham gave [when that one moved from WebDriver to HTML](https://github.com/w3c/webdriver/pull/1695#issuecomment-1339661667).\n\nMy plan would be foolip's straw proposal:  it takes only a direction and returns when the action is complete (which elements are sequentially focusable would be a separate setting).\n\n@jgraham, would Mozilla support this, and is a Classic command enough on its own, or should there also be a BiDi one?\n\n@annevk, would WebKit support this, and should the standardized WebDriver toggle you [suggested](https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/171#issuecomment-4199418777) for macOS's keyboard navigation setting be specified together with it? (cc @janewman, who [asked about one](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11723#issuecomment-4317488764) for focusgroup)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
